WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:13.997
flag marks selected categories. scanFlags forms exclusive offsets using staged shared-memory scans and collective barriers. scatter writes original token IDs at those unique offsets.

00:00:14.217 --> 00:00:19.551
All three kernels are ordered in one stream; main verifies the complete stable result.

00:00:21.571 --> 00:00:22.787
Flag tokens.

00:00:23.007 --> 00:00:25.119
Record whether each token survives.

00:00:25.339 --> 00:00:26.491
Scan flags.

00:00:26.711 --> 00:00:29.399
Form exclusive offsets with shared stages.

00:00:29.619 --> 00:00:31.091
Scatter IDs.

00:00:31.311 --> 00:00:33.295
Write each selected token once.

00:00:35.315 --> 00:00:39.923
Flags produced in device memory must be ready before scatter consumes them.

00:00:40.143 --> 00:00:43.940
Unique offsets give selected threads distinct destinations.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:49.088
Stable output order follows the offsets, not the order in which warps happen to run.
